{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_4He","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_4He","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_4He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_4He","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_4He.lean#L25-L38","doc":"**Pauli witness for ${}^{4}\\mathrm{He}$** ($Z=2$, $N=2$, $A=4$),\ndoubly magic.\n\nThe exact Gröbner normal form in $H_4(q)$ after quotient ideals\n$I_8 + I_9$ gives $F_{\\mathrm{Pauli}}^{(4)} \\approx 0.812$.  The\npolynomial $\\mathrm{net}(t)$ has $[2]_t^2 \\cdot [3]_t = 2^2 \\cdot 3 = 12$\nterms in $\\mathbb{Z}[t, t^{-1}]$.  The combinatorial count and magic\nnumbers are discharged by computation; the empirical Pauli factor is the\nsingle conjectural input carried by `[Witness4HePauli]`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:witness-4he","label":"def:witness-4he","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-nf-witnesses/witness-4he.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli.pauli_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli.pauli_approx","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_4He.lean#L23-L23","doc":"The `H₄(q)` Gröbner normal form yields `F_Pauli ≈ 0.812`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli.F_Pauli","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli.F_Pauli","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_4He.lean#L21-L21","doc":"Pauli witness `F_Pauli^{(4)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli.mk","kind":"ctor","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_4He.lean#L19-L19","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness4HePauli","kind":"class","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_4He.lean#L16-L23","doc":"The one genuinely-open input for the ⁴He witness: the empirical Pauli\nfactor `F_Pauli^{(4)} ≈ 0.812` from the `H₄(q)` Gröbner normal form\n(a categorical derivation of the value is open). ","signatureChunk":0}]}